id: pm-github-9cjx
title: Reach exact all-source coverage and include every operational script
description: "The unchanged all-source gate now measures exact 100 percent lines, statements, branches and functions across all 12 authored TypeScript/JavaScript modules, including operational scripts. The frozen full npm coverage run passes 487 tests with zero failures or skips. Real Git, PM SDK, filesystem and HTTP cases cover reachable paths; removed private-path arms have invariant proofs recorded in comments and docs/coverage-gap-inventory.md. No source ignores or lowered thresholds. Final npm/Bun release receipts and orchestrator review remain separate."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[5]: all-source,coverage,quality-gate,scripts,tdd
created_at: "2026-08-17T07:32:29.666Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-06T14:33:49.525Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "Automatically discover every executable TypeScript production and operational source; require exact 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines; prohibit ignore pragmas, source allowlist blind spots, threshold weakening, vacuous tests, and mocks of the unit under test; exercise GitHub behavior at the HTTP boundary, pm behavior through real SDK/installed-CLI boundaries, and operational scripts through real filesystem/process behavior; prove the gate fails when a new uncovered source or branch is introduced."
unblock_note: Full source coverage closure is being reverified at unchanged exact thresholds.
expected_result: "Every executable TypeScript source and operational script is automatically included in measurement and exact statements, branches, functions, and lines all reach 100% through behavioral tests."
actual_result: Fresh npm and Bun release gates at f572382 pass 503/503 tests with exact all-source 100/100/100/100 across 12 modules. Lines/statements 8406/8406; Node 22 functions 209/209 and branches 2226/2226; Node 26 functions 208/208 and branches 2225/2225. Exact-100 gate passes. CI Node 22/26 and native Bun pass; full native linked changelog/privacy tests pass 29/29.
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-github-n3z3,related,"2026-08-17T07:32:29.666Z",codex,"cli:create:dep",detected
comments[34]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T07:52:16.974Z",codex-sol,"Replaced the narrowed coverage wrapper with an explicit authored-module inventory, exact 100 percent thresholds for all four dimensions, stale-LCOV invalidation, and missing-file rejection. Added checked operational-script tests, ESLint enforcement, erasable TypeScript syntax, and a jscpd wrapper that verifies its full source inventory. Typecheck, 122 documented declarations, ESLint, and zero duplication passed. Coverage remains a measured gate rather than an approval claim."
  "2026-10-05T08:09:10.457Z",codex-sol,"Strict all-authored-module run completed with 369 tests passing and no skipped tests. Coverage remained below the unchanged 100/100/100/100 requirement: lines/statements 93.25 percent, branches 84.41 percent, functions 94.92 percent over 11 authored TS/JS modules including operational scripts. LCOV was invalidated on failure. Most remaining uncovered branches and ten uncovered functions are in the pre-existing GitHub Projects sync handlers; this is a release blocker, not a passing gate. The shell release-date verifier remains outside the V8 denominator and is exercised separately."
  "2026-10-05T08:58:34.554Z",codex-sol,"Final frozen-source verification at 0b7c4ab: the linked npm coverage command ran all 375 tests with 375 passing, zero failures and zero skips, then correctly exited nonzero at the unchanged 100 percent gate. Complete inventory: 12 authored TS/JS modules including operational scripts. Lines/statements 7739 of 8285 = 93.40 percent; branches 1548 of 1826 = 84.77 percent; functions 188 of 198 = 94.94 percent. Failed LCOV was removed. No source ignores or lowered thresholds were introduced; release remains blocked."
  "2026-10-05T09:09:52.779Z",codex-sol-coverage,"Resuming the existing strict 12-module coverage implementation. Iteration will use targeted Node and c8 runs, real scratch PM and git projects, and SDK extension harness behavior tests. The complete npm coverage gate is reserved for the orchestrator. Existing unrelated tracker edits are preserved. First priority is Projects sync and apply behavior, then remaining planner and operational failure boundaries."
  "2026-10-05T09:18:20.026Z",codex-sol-coverage,"Added 18 behavior cases for Projects sync and planners. Targeted Node c8 execution passed 51 of 51 tests, zero skips. Verified preview-only and scoped execution, dry-run override, both conflict preferences, draft and issue mutations, lifecycle close and cancellation metadata, partial and total failures, and a real concurrent local deletion after remote attachment. PM tag ordering is normalized, so the preservation assertion checks membership. No production behavior, dependencies, thresholds, or source inventory changed."
  "2026-10-05T09:26:42.190Z",codex-sol-coverage,"Native Bun verification passed all 12 Projects harness cases and all 39 planner cases, with per-file timeout 600000. Executable lookup failure fixtures now run in explicit Node subprocesses while registered harness behavior stays native. This follows the existing lifecycle test boundary and prevents temporary PATH changes from reaching the host credential helper. Linked Node tests passed 51 of 51 through pm test; test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment records the receipt."
  "2026-10-05T09:29:20.437Z",codex-sol-coverage,"The Projects planner module now measures exact 100/100/100/100 in the targeted c8 run: 732 of 732 lines and statements, 18 of 18 functions, 181 of 181 branches, with 39 Node tests passing. Removed only the impossible parse-exception catch after validating even-length hex; Buffer accepts that validated input without a parsing exception. Malformed encodings still reject before decoding, and uppercase hex preserves the original case-sensitive id. Full package evidence remains pending the orchestrator run; saved baseline receipts cannot be treated as exact-current after scanner changes by the parallel review work."
  "2026-10-05T09:31:52.268Z",codex-sol-coverage,"Counter correction for the latest Projects-only run: all 182 of 182 measured branches are covered; the prior comment used the earlier branch total of 181. Lines and statements remain 732 of 732, functions 18 of 18. The linked 39-test Node planner suite passed. Added eight additional real filesystem/process boundary cases; targeted Node and native Bun both pass 8 of 8."
  "2026-10-05T09:34:52.514Z",codex-sol,"Stopped the Codex CLI coverage sub-agent immediately after a fresh quota check reported OVER_FORECAST while the other providers remained exhausted, honoring the owner weekly forecast limit. Preserved its focused commits and remaining test files for orchestrator verification. Projects planners reached exact 100 in targeted c8; 12 Projects harness cases, 8 operational boundary cases, and 9 import error cases passed Node and native Bun. Package-wide coverage still requires a fresh frozen-source run and must not be presented as 100. No thresholds, source inventory, or ignores were weakened."
  "2026-10-05T09:41:56.169Z",codex-sol,"Orchestrator verification preserved the interrupted new coverage tests and corrected their fixture setup: explicit repo-local tracker initialization, filename-derived item id expectations, and removal of the linked host package-root environment for the missing-metadata Windows case. The preserved Projects and planner cases pass Node; all 74 preserved cases pass native Bun. The newly linked boundary/import/diff command is being reverified through the PM runner before final broad checks. These are test-fixture corrections; production rejection behavior and the exact gate remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-05T09:45:17.622Z",codex-sol,The corrected linked boundary/import/diff command passes all 23 Node cases through pm test with progress and exit zero. The preserved Projects/planner suites also passed their native behavior checks; the complete 74-case preserved set passed Bun before the environment-isolation correction. Final frozen-source full npm coverage and native Bun checks follow. All useful interrupted files are retained and linked to this item.
  "2026-10-06T11:13:02.345Z",codex-sol,"Continuing the interrupted work on the same branch. Reviewing every preserved production change against its invariants, measuring all-source coverage, and adding real Git, filesystem, HTTP, and SDK behavior tests. Exact thresholds stay at 100 in all four dimensions; no ignore pragmas or inventory exclusions. PR 108 already exists and will receive the final measured receipts."
  "2026-10-06T11:17:43.296Z",codex-sol,"Reviewed the preserved simplifications. Proofs for removed impossible arms: phone regexes guarantee digits; a context-line branch guarantees its leading space; successful encoded spawnSync gives string stdout/stderr while startup failures populate error; fixed valid spawn arguments report missing tools via error/status rather than throwing; nullish SDK fallbacks execute only for a missing injection; fetchJSON resolves only for 2xx; split on a string always returns at least one element; SDK command/import/preflight/search contexts require their arguments and options. Scanner operations on decoded plain strings and arrays have only the explicit malformed-history GateInputError. Restored the formatGateReport empty-field fallback because its exported typed input can contain an empty string. Fixing fixture setup and replacing an always-true assertion; no thresholds or ignores changed."
  "2026-10-06T11:33:54.300Z",codex-sol,"The second complete npm run passes all 471 tests with zero skips. Coverage is 99.80 percent lines/statements, 97.74 percent branches, and 100 percent functions. Every operational script and gate.ts now measure exact 100 in all dimensions. Remaining index.ts gaps are enumerated from the JSON receipt. Centralizing thrown-value formatting and the identical command gate error boundary preserves behavior while removing duplicated decisions; real collaborator errors are still redacted and fail closed. Additional proven unreachable arms: a search loop cannot execute with an empty match array; fixed gh version spawn reports failures in its result; an atomic dry-run returns before the non-atomic preview; the private Projects add-issue executor receives coordinates populated by its sole planner. Tests retain defaults exposed by public planners."
  "2026-10-06T11:40:59.548Z",codex-sol,"Third full coverage run: all 484 tests pass; statements, lines and functions are 100%, branches 99.59%. Nine remaining branch locations enumerated from coverage-final.json. Proof for deleting two private-path fallbacks: applyPushEntry receives only planner entries; existing project item indices reject empty ids, and both gqlAddDraft and gqlAddIssue throw before returning an empty id (real GraphQL missing-id tests verify this). The redundant no-item-id guard cannot execute. Pull statusSkipped is appended only inside if(pi.statusName), assigning optionName that same truthy string, so its missing-name fallback cannot execute. Complete PM reads validate tags and body/description strings; the private executor only looks up ids from that complete selected corpus. No coverage exclusions or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-06T11:43:22.121Z",codex-sol,"The targeted real-command c8 check passes four tests: low unauthenticated quota, human Projects listings, after-command subprocess boundaries, and all four Projects mutation failure boundaries. It covers the remaining reachable branches, including open-board formatting and missing tags. The complete npm release check and all native Bun test files are now running on frozen source. docs/coverage-gap-inventory.md retains every initial uncovered statement and branch plus the final nine-branch inventory and closure proofs."
  "2026-10-06T11:49:57.012Z",codex-sol,"Frozen full npm coverage PASS: 487 tests, zero failures/skips; all 12 authored modules measure exact 100/100/100/100. JSON receipt has zero uncovered statements or branches. Production dependency audit passes with zero vulnerabilities. The linked PM planner command passes all 39 tests through pm test --run --progress; the linked watchdog command previously passed through the PM runner. Full release completion and native Bun verification follow."
  "2026-10-06T11:55:39.390Z",codex-sol,"The first exact-100 full npm release check passed at implementation 40db9b3. Broad native testing then exposed a real HTTP timeout regression, recorded in hptv and fixed without raising deadlines. Source is re-frozen for full npm and native Bun verification; earlier coverage receipts are not claimed for the transport change until remeasured."
  "2026-10-06T12:03:40.399Z",codex-sol,"Full npm release:check at transport-fix implementation 5ed8c47 PASS: 487 tests with zero failures/skips; exact 100/100/100/100 across all 12 authored modules. No uncovered statement or branch counters remain. All release static gates, Git-object privacy, production dependency audit, packing, changelog and publish attestation pass. Starting the full Bun-invoked release command on this same implementation; native Bun full-suite timeout regression already passes at 30.04 seconds."
  "2026-10-06T12:07:15.906Z",codex-sol,"Four native lock fixture failures are a test-runner API mismatch: Bun 1.3.5 does not implement node:test mock.method. Replacing only syscall-boundary replacement/restoration with a small explicit helper, retaining real temporary lock files, permission changes, live-peer protection and the same injected I/O failures. Also close the real descriptor after the simulated close failure so the fixture leaves no open descriptor. Production source and coverage thresholds are unchanged; focused Node and native Bun checks are running."
  "2026-10-06T12:08:41.954Z",codex-sol,"All four corrected lock boundary cases pass both Node and native Bun (4/4 each), with the same real filesystem and live-peer assertions. Build:test passes. Production source remains exactly 5ed8c47. The superseded native run with known mock.method fixture failures has been stopped; restarting the entire 30-file native suite with portable fixtures and verifying the complete 24-case Node lock file. The full Bun release command continues on the unchanged production source."
  "2026-10-06T12:19:41.403Z",codex-sol,"The complete native rerun exposed two remaining fixture lookup failures: Bun caches executable resolution at startup, so changing process.env.PATH later does not reliably redirect git. These privacy-gate negative controls now launch the same runtime in a real child with the intended PATH from startup, retaining real Git repositories, malformed inventory and failed blob-read assertions. Production sources remain byte-identical to 5ed8c47; no gate logic, ignores or thresholds change. Full 25-case Node/Bun privacy files are being verified before the final native rerun."
  "2026-10-06T12:20:40.769Z",codex-sol,"The startup-environment privacy fixture confirms an additional Bun lookup detail: an empty PATH falls back to default tool lookup. Using a nonempty scratch directory with no executable git makes the missing-tool case real under both runtimes. Malformed inventory and failed blob-read controls already pass in the native child; the complete Node privacy file passes 25/25. Retrying the full native privacy file with the empty-directory PATH, preserving the actual production gate and real Git fixtures."
  "2026-10-06T12:22:15.502Z",codex-sol,"Portable privacy fixtures now pass the complete 25-case native Bun file; the complete Node privacy file passes 25/25, and its final two startup-lookup cases pass again after the empty-directory PATH correction. ESLint and build:test pass. Starting the final complete native suite and a fresh npm coverage run with every final fixture, ensuring child-process coverage counters remain complete. Production implementation remains byte-identical to 5ed8c47."
  "2026-10-06T12:31:03.576Z",codex-sol,"Final fresh npm coverage with all portable fixtures PASS: 487 tests, zero failures/skips; exact 100/100/100/100 across all 12 authored modules, 8398 lines/statements, 2219 branches and 208 functions. JSON contains zero uncovered statement/branch counters. The real same-runtime child fixtures preserve V8 coverage evidence. Complete npm and Bun release checks already pass on identical production sources; the final native suite remains in progress with no failures."
  "2026-10-06T12:31:38.843Z",codex-sol,"Counter correction for the final portable-fixture npm coverage receipt: it contains 2220/2220 covered branches, not 2219. Earlier complete release receipts contain 2219/2219. Both retain all 12 modules, exact 100 percent, zero uncovered counters and zero skipped source. Final lines/statements are 8398/8398 and functions 208/208. Production source is unchanged; the latest receipt is authoritative for the final fixture run."
  "2026-10-06T12:33:58.453Z",codex-sol,"The complete native suite has all 487 cases passing across 30 files with zero failed assertions, but its shell result is nonzero. Isolated duplication-gate file reproduces exit one despite 3/3 passing: the script-entry negative control sets process.exitCode=1, and restoring undefined does not clear it under Bun. Four touched entry fixtures now restore previous ?? 0, matching existing docstring/attestation fixture practice. Production source remains unchanged. Checking each affected file exit status and restarting native acceptance to require exit zero as well as zero failed cases."
  "2026-10-06T12:35:41.764Z",codex-sol,"Exit cleanup verified: all four affected Bun entry-fixture files now return process exit zero with zero failed tests; the combined 38-case Node run also passes with zero skips, and lint/build:test pass. The previous complete native run already passed all 487 assertions across 30 files. Running the complete native command once more to obtain an explicit exit-zero receipt. Production code remains unchanged, with final full coverage exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-10-06T12:42:45.910Z",codex-sol,"Final native command npm run test:bun PASS with process exit zero: 487 passing cases across all 30 files, zero failed cases. Final source coverage is exact 100/100/100/100 across all 12 authored modules with no ignores/lowered thresholds and no uncovered counters. The complete npm/Bun release checks pass; final fixture-only changes retain byte-identical production implementation 5ed8c47. Portable syscall, startup-PATH and explicit exit-code cleanup fixtures now work under both runtimes. Claims will be released and the item remains open for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-06T13:55:53.428Z",codex-sol,"Historical actual_result described ae86e7d: 420 tests passed but coverage was 97.59 percent lines/statements, 89.24 percent branches, 100 percent functions and exact-100 failed. The latest pushed baseline a849280 subsequently passed exact all-source 100/100/100/100 in fresh clones; replacing the stale current field, with review-round-1 verification pending."
  "2026-10-06T14:00:16.233Z",codex-sol,"Review regressions verified red/green for all 16 findings. Linked focused pm test commands pass 8 tests each; result persistence is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment records the receipt. Build:test, ESLint, 130 documented declarations and zero duplication across all 12 authored modules pass. Canonicalization required replacing nonexistent mocked directories in two prior Git failure tests with real fixture directories; their intended status and containment refusal branches pass."
  "2026-10-06T14:10:31.229Z",codex-sol,"Persistent revert receipts: 4196078345 current coverage task field; 4196078470 README anchor; 4196078483 in-repository dot-dot source name; 4196078520 changelog spawn/signal diagnostics; 4196078539 historical provenance Git diagnostic; 4196078563 permission cleanup after a forced sync throw; 4196078603 complete secret literal refusal; 4196078637 explicit gate override. Each reviewed-code negative control failed and restored code passed. No finding was declined. Existing exact-100 source inventory, thresholds and exclusions are unchanged."
  "2026-10-06T14:20:36.531Z",codex-sol,"Fresh-clone release gates at c8b9329 PASS: 503 tests, exact all-source 100/100/100/100, 130 documented declarations, zero duplication, lint, typecheck, privacy, zero production audit vulnerabilities, package dry-run, changelog check and publish attestation. Latest coverage receipts replace the historical failed actual_result; previous measurements remain in comments/history. The portable diagnostic fixture has another failing revert/passing restore proof, and focused Node/native Bun verification passes. Preparing final receipt commit and exact pushed-head clones."
  "2026-10-06T14:33:48.844Z",codex-sol,"Final source/test head f572382 passes fresh npm and Bun release checks: 503/503 tests, exact 100/100/100/100 across 12 modules, 8406/8406 lines/statements; Node 22 has 209/209 functions and 2226/2226 branches, Node 26 has 208/208 functions and 2225/2225 branches. CI test (22) and test (26) pass including the full native Bun suite. Replaced the filtered native linked command after the pinned PM runner falsely classified two passing Bun tests as empty; full native changelog/privacy files pass 29/29 through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Separate follow-up pm-github-2ao1 preserves that upstream limitation; no package source or coverage policy workaround was added."
